employee_hdl() wired into startup seeds. Verified: py_compile clean, JSON valid, and a unit test renders every component block correctly (42736->2017/01/01, Spain->ES, Employee->E, keys + manager parse). Still needs a live end-to-end run on the app (create an Employee HDL conversion on a Workday extract -> Generate -> inspect the .dat zip). (C) SUPPLIER TRANSFORMS (from Raman's BA feedback / internal review): supplier_transform_mappings.json + seed_supplier_transform_mappings() seed the transform rows the analysts flagged, across Supplier / Supplier Address / Supplier Site. Delivery Method AND Delivery Channel are now DERIVED via CASE_WHEN from the Email/Fax Transaction flags (Email=Yes->EMAIL, Fax=Yes->FAX, else blank) instead of a forced constant. Phone (Address) and Fax (Address + Site) are SPLIT into their Country Code / Area Code / Extension / Number FBDI columns via a new PHONE_PART transform rule (added to the engine + RULE_TYPES) that parses +cc/00, area group and ext deterministically. Use Withholding Tax <- Default WT Code. Engine fix: _transform_frame now keeps and exposes columns referenced by CASE_WHEN/CONCAT/COALESCE rules (via _rule_referenced_columns) so a derivation reading a non-mapped column (e.g. the transaction flags) no longer silently sees blanks; these columns also survive the wide-source pruning. Target field names verified against the parsed supplier templates. Source column names (Email Transactions, Fax Transactions, Phone, Fax, Default WT Code) are BEST-GUESS defaults flagged in the JSON _note - verify against the All Vendors extract. Unit-tested: PHONE_PART and CASE_WHEN produce the expected values. (D) MULTI-TENANCY / CLIENT SCOPING: everything the tool learns is now grouped by CLIENT so a future client never inherits NextPower's source-system assumptions, while Oracle-standard knowledge stays global. New Client entity (app/models/client.py, registered in Beanie) + client_id/is_global on LearnedMapping, GoldStandard, FBDITemplate and client_id on Project. client_service.py centralises resolution (client_id_for_conversion via project) and scoping: scope_query returns 'this client OR global', and for the DEFAULT (NextPower) client also includes legacy/untagged rows so nothing regresses. Reads scoped: apply_learned_to_conversion (column_mapping/suppress/example_default) and the map-time learned-targets query in mapping_service. Captures tagged client-scoped (is_global=False): _upsert_learned + capture_learnings_from_conversion, gold reference standards and the GoldStandard record itself. Seeders: FBDI/HDL templates + the public-schema mapping_catalog seed GLOBAL; the NextPower analyst mappings (item/supplier/customer/HDL) + supplier transforms scope to the seeded NextPower client. Idempotent startup migration (run_client_scope_migration) tags all pre-existing data: templates+catalog global, every other learning/gold/project -> NextPower; only touches untagged rows so it's a no-op thereafter and never re-globalises a client template. New /api/clients CRUD + per-client knowledge counts; client_id/is_global now serialise on learnings/gold/templates responses. Frontend: ClientsApi + a Clients page (per-client counts + a Global group + add-client/set-default) wired into the router and sidebar. Backend py_compile clean; new frontend files type-check clean (repo has pre-existing tsc noise, builds via Vite). live smoke test recommended after deploy. (E) CLIENT-FILTERED VIEWS + read scoping: /learned-mappings and /by-object accept a client_id filter ('global' or an id); /gold list accepts client_id and returns client_id; effective-defaults now scoped to the conversion's client. Learning Center gets a client filter dropdown (All / Global only / each client) that scopes both the by-object groups and the drill-down rows. (F) SINGLE<->MULTI COLUMN MAPPING UI: a 'Split / combine' modal in Mapping Review lets users map ONE source column to MANY fields (phone/fax -> Country/Area/Extension/Number via PHONE_PART, or split-by-delimiter via SPLIT) and MANY source columns into ONE field (CONCAT), wired through MappingApi.update/addRule + suggested_transformation so it flows straight into Generate. Backend py_compile clean; new frontend code type-checks clean (repo tsc baseline unchanged). Remaining fast-follows: reset-defaults + value-map recommend scoping, gold-upload client picker, Templates/Gold page client filters. (G) SUPPLIER EMAIL MASKING + CUSTOMER TEMPLATE: supplier loads now neutralise e-mail addresses so a migration/test load can't fire real supplier/contact notifications - a generation-time mask prefixes every non-blank e-mail-named column of a Supplier object with 'xx' (idempotent, skips blanks/nulls), plus new reusable PREFIX/SUFFIX transform rule types. Unit-tested. Also refreshed the bundled Customer Import template with the client-provided CustomerImportTemplate.xlsm (parses to the full 19 HZ_IMP/RA sheets / 1254 fields; wired via the existing _BUNDLED entry + ensure_customer_multisheet, idempotent). (H) ITEM MAPPING QUALITY + FBDI VALIDATION (BA feedback, Item import): map-time guard on Item conversions (mapping_service._guard_item_mappings) drops a numeric source landing in a text Name/Description field (e.g. a code mis-mapped into 'Item Class Name') and flags one source column being copied across multiple fields for review - so the matcher stops blindly populating with fuzzy/direct-copy noise. Validation engine (validation/engine.run_validation_checks) extended with Oracle FBDI rules using the parsed field metadata: value-set/LOV enforcement (value must be an allowed_values code - e.g. Inventory Planning Method can't hold an org code), Numeric-Value-In-Text-Field (bare number in a *Name* field), Negative-Value-Not-Allowed on quantity/on-hand/weight fields, and the related-field Min<=Max business rule (Minimum Order Quantity must not exceed Maximum). quality_service now passes allowed_values so LOV checks run. All new checks + the guard are unit-tested. Remaining (needs Oracle value-set data via a Manage-Standard-Lookups import): full enumerated-value coverage for instance-configurable LOVs whose codes aren't in the template. (I) CLIENTS ENDPOINT HARDENING + TARGET-FBDI FILTER: /api/clients is now fully guarded - a runtime error returns a clean 503 (which carries CORS headers) instead of an unhandled 500 that Starlette serves OUTSIDE the CORS middleware (that was surfacing in the browser as an opaque 'blocked by CORS policy' + ERR_FAILED); per-client counts use a _safe_count that can't throw. Learning Center gains a second filter dropdown ('All target FBDI' -> each object) alongside the client filter, so learnings can be narrowed by target object as well as client. NextPower remains the default client (ensure_default_client + the one-time migration seed it and tag all analyst rules to it). (J) CRITICAL FIX + target filter + AI steering: (1) ROOT CAUSE of the Clients 503 / effective-defaults CORS errors - the Client model was imported into database.py but NOT added to init_beanie(document_models=[...]), so every Client query raised CollectionWasNotInitialized. Client is now registered; default_client_id() is also hardened to never throw (falls back to permissive scope) so a tenant hiccup can't break mapping/generate. (2) Mapping Review canvas now has a 'Filter target FBDI fields...' box mirroring the source filter (tgtQuery), with a match count and no-match message. (3) Steering box ('Learn & apply') now takes plain English: lines the regex can't parse are sent to the Claude API (_ai_parse_directives) which returns structured map/default/suppress directives against the real field list; every steering directive (regex OR AI) is now stored as a reusable CLIENT-SCOPED learned rule (column_mapping / example_default / suppress_field tagged with the conversion's client_id) so it persists for that client and never leaks to others. All backend compiles; frontend target filter type-checks clean. Re-run launch_git and the Clients page + effective-defaults will work once the backend redeploys."
